.TH CLAUDE 1 "April 2026" "haiku-claude-cli" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
claude \- command-line client for Anthropic's Claude on Haiku
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B claude
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ MESSAGE ...]
.br
.B claude
.I login
.br
.B claude
.I logout
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B claude
is a native Haiku command-line client for Anthropic's Claude API with
streaming responses, OAuth 2.0 authentication against claude.ai (Pro/Max
subscription) or API-key authentication, an interactive REPL, built-in
tools (Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Glob, Grep, WebFetch, WebSearch, Task,
TodoWrite/TodoRead), MCP (Model Context Protocol) server integration,
shell-command lifecycle hooks, project memory via
.IR CLAUDE.md ,
custom slash commands, and more.
.PP
Running
.B claude
with no arguments in a terminal drops directly into interactive mode.
In a non-interactive context (pipe, redirect, cron), a message must be
provided on the command line or piped in via stdin.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B login
Authenticate against claude.ai using OAuth 2.0 + PKCE. Opens a browser
for authorization and saves the returned tokens to
.IR ~/config/settings/claude-cli/credentials.json .
.TP
.B logout
Delete the stored OAuth credentials.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-i, \-\-interactive
Start a multi-turn REPL session (the default when
.B claude
is invoked with no message at a terminal).
.TP
.BI \-m " MODEL" ", \-\-model " MODEL
Override the default model (claude-sonnet-4-6).
.TP
.BI \-t " N" ", \-\-max-tokens " N
Set the maximum tokens in the response (default 1024).
.TP
.BI \-s " TEXT" ", \-\-system " TEXT
Append a custom system prompt. With OAuth, the required Claude Code
preamble is preserved and this text is appended after it.
.TP
.B \-u, \-\-usage
After a one-shot response, print input/output token counts to stderr.
.TP
.B \-r, \-\-resume
Pre-load the REPL with the last saved session (implies
.BR \-i ).
.TP
.B \-y, \-\-yes
Auto-approve destructive tools
.RB ( Bash ", " Write ", " Edit )
for this invocation without prompting. Required for one-shot runs
where stdin is not a terminal (piped, redirected, or inside a
subprocess); otherwise the y/a/n dialog has no way to get an
answer and the tool is denied with a clear error. Equivalent to
.I allow_destructive_tools: true
in the config file, but scoped to a single run.
.TP
.B \-\-plain
Disable ANSI color output.
.TP
.B \-\-color
Force ANSI color output even when piped.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH SLASH COMMANDS
Inside the REPL:
.TP
.B /help
Show the list of slash commands (built-in and custom).
.TP
.B /clear
Reset the running conversation.
.TP
.BI /model " NAME"
Swap the active model mid-session.
.TP
.B /compact
Ask Claude to summarize the running history and replace it with the
summary.
.TP
.B /cost
Session token cost estimate based on the config's price table.
.TP
.B /todos
Show the current in-session todo list.
.TP
.BR /memory " [user]"
Open the project or user
.I CLAUDE.md
in
.B $EDITOR
(falls back to nano). Memory is reloaded on the next turn.
.TP
.B /exit, /quit
Leave the REPL (Ctrl+D also works).
.PP
User-defined slash commands may live in
.I .claude/commands/*.md
(project) or
.I ~/config/settings/claude-cli/commands/*.md
(user). The filename minus
.I .md
becomes the command name; the body is a prompt template with
.I {{args}}
substituted from the text following the command invocation.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.B claude
reads an optional JSON config file at
.IR ~/config/settings/claude-cli/config.json .
Recognized keys:
.TP
.I model
Default model string.
.TP
.I max_tokens
Default response token cap.
.TP
.I system
Default custom system prompt.
.TP
.I show_usage
Boolean; default for
.BR \-\-usage .
.TP
.I allow_destructive_tools
Boolean; when
.BR true ,
.BR Bash ", " Write ", and " Edit
skip the interactive permission prompt. Useful for headless or
piped-stdin runs where no y/a/n dialog is possible. Equivalent to
passing
.B \-y/\-\-yes
on every invocation.
.TP
.I prices
Object keyed by model name with
.RB { input ", " output }
per-million-token prices (dollars) for
.BR /cost .
.TP
.I hooks
Object keyed by event name with arrays of
.RB { matcher ?, command }
entries. Event names:
.BR SessionStart ,
.BR UserPromptSubmit ,
.BR PreToolUse ,
.BR PostToolUse ,
.BR Stop .
Each hook runs as
.IR "sh -c <command>"
with a JSON event payload on stdin. A non-zero exit blocks the next
action.
.TP
.I mcp_servers
Object keyed by server name with
.RB { command ", " args ", " env }
entries. Each named server is spawned as a subprocess over stdio
JSON-RPC 2.0, initialized via the MCP handshake, and its tools are
advertised to Claude as
.IR mcp__<server>__<tool> .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/config/settings/claude-cli/config.json
Per-user configuration.
.TP
.I ~/config/settings/claude-cli/credentials.json
OAuth tokens (0600).
.TP
.I ~/config/settings/claude-cli/history.json
Most recent REPL conversation history for
.BR \-\-resume .
.TP
.I ~/config/settings/claude-cli/repl_history
Persistent line-editing history for the REPL prompt.
.TP
.I ~/config/settings/claude-cli/CLAUDE.md
User-level project memory.
.TP
.I ./CLAUDE.md
Project memory loaded from the current working directory.
.TP
.I .claude/commands/*.md
Project-scoped custom slash commands.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
Falls back to API-key billing when no OAuth tokens are stored.
.TP
.B BRAVE_SEARCH_API_KEY
Enables the WebSearch tool via the Brave Search API.
.TP
.B EDITOR
Editor launched by the
.B /memory
slash command.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR, CLICOLOR, TERM
Honored by the ANSI-color detection.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Overrides the user config directory location on non-Haiku builds.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
One-shot query:
.PP
.RS
.nf
claude "Give me a one-paragraph history of BeOS."
.fi
.RE
.PP
Pipe context in:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cat README.md | claude "Summarize this in three bullets."
.fi
.RE
.PP
Interactive session resumed from last time:
.PP
.RS
.nf
claude \-r
.fi
.RE
